  faqs: [
    { question: "Does any school in Barpeta teach the IB or IGCSE?", answer: "We could not confirm any school in Barpeta offering the IB or a Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel IGCSE. Local schools, including the district's Kendriya Vidyalaya and Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalaya, follow CBSE or the Assam state board. The nearest confirmed IGCSE school is in Guwahati, about 90 km away, and the nearest IB schools are in Kolkata, so most families add online tuition to their present school." },
    { question: "Will an IB Gram tutor come to my house in Barpeta?", answer: "No, tutors do not visit homes in Barpeta. In-person home tuition runs only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. In Barpeta your child studies from home on a laptop while the tutor teaches live over video with a shared whiteboard, which is private one-to-one tuition in every respect except the tutor being in the room." },
    { question: "How do I start looking for an IB tutor in Barpeta?", answer: "Send a short brief with the programme, subject, level, current grade and exam session, and we propose tutors who have taught that exact course. Since Barpeta has no pool of local IB teachers, the search is national. You then sit a free trial lesson online and decide. If the tutor does not suit, we suggest another without any awkwardness." },
    { question: "Can a student in Barpeta sit IGCSE exams without changing school?", answer: "Usually yes, as a private candidate. You choose Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel, confirm the syllabus code and tier, and register through an authorised exam centre before its deadline; centres are often in Guwahati. Tuition happens online and does not touch the school timetable. Ask about centre places early, since availability and dates vary." },
    { question: "How much does online IB or IGCSE tuition cost for Barpeta families?", answer: "There is no published rate card. The cost depends on the programme and level, session length and frequency, and the tutor's experience with your exact syllabus, and the figure is sent in writing before you book. Living in Barpeta instead of Guwahati changes nothing, because every lesson is online, and the free trial comes before any commitment." },
    { question: "What happens in the free trial lesson?", answer: "Your child works through a genuine topic from their syllabus with the proposed tutor on video, at no charge and with no obligation. The tutor watches how the student thinks, asks diagnostic questions and explains a concept or two. Afterwards you receive a first-month plan and the written rate, and you choose whether to continue, adjust or try someone else." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with my IB Internal Assessment or Extended Essay?", answer: "A tutor can coach the process but never writes any part of the work. Help includes understanding the criteria, refining a research question, planning data collection and giving honest feedback on a draft. Writing, rewriting or supplying content for assessed work breaches IB integrity rules and puts the qualification at risk, so it is not offered." },
    { question: "My child studies in an Assamese-medium or Bengali-medium school. Can IB or IGCSE tuition still work?", answer: "Yes, provided the plan allows time for academic English. The content is learnable in any language of schooling, but IB and IGCSE answers must be written precisely in English. Tutors build a glossary of core terms, teach command words explicitly and set short written explanations each week, so language improves alongside subject knowledge." },
    { question: "Which IB subjects can be matched for a student in Barpeta?", answer: "Most Diploma subjects can be matched, including both Maths courses, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, Computer Science, Psychology, Geography, English A, Hindi B and Theory of Knowledge. Bengali A: Literature is confirmed at the brief stage. Tell us the subject, level and exam session, and we will say honestly whether a specialist is available." },
    { question: "Do you teach younger students in IB PYP and MYP?", answer: "Yes. PYP tutoring covers reading, writing, number sense and inquiry habits in short regular sessions. MYP tutoring focuses on criterion-based tasks in Sciences, Mathematics and Language and Literature, and on keeping a good process journal for the Personal Project. Without a local IB school, the tutor often supplies the programme-specific routines a transferred child would otherwise lose." },
    { question: "What if floods or a power cut interrupt an online lesson?", answer: "Tell the tutor as soon as you can and rejoin when the connection returns; a phone hotspot is a sensible backup. Interrupted sessions can usually be made up by agreeing another slot that week. Flood-season spells are the likeliest cause, so Internal Assessment drafts and mock papers are best finished a few days ahead of any deadline." },
    { question: "When is the right time to begin IB Diploma or IGCSE tuition in Barpeta?", answer: "The best time is the start of the course: Class 11 for the Diploma and Grade 9 for IGCSE. Early weeks build academic English, command-word habits and the first Internal Assessment plans while there is time to correct course. Beginning later still helps, with the tutor focusing on the highest-value topics and timed papers for the next series." },
    { question: "Can my child prepare for JEE or NEET while studying IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Many students try, and it can work with a realistic timetable. IB Physics, Chemistry, Biology and Maths overlap with JEE and NEET topics, but question styles differ, so each needs its own practice. We tutor the IB or IGCSE side; entrance coaching is separate. Check current eligibility rules for your board before committing to both." },
    { question: "Is Cambridge or Edexcel more practical for a private candidate in Assam?", answer: "It depends on which board has exam-centre places, dates and subject options that suit you, so ask early in Guwahati. Both are recognised worldwide and cover similar content. Cambridge sits in May-June and October-November; Edexcel sits in January and May-June. Whichever you choose, keep every practice paper on that board." },
    { question: "Will Indian universities accept IB or IGCSE results from an Assam student?", answer: "Yes, through equivalence and entrance routes. The Association of Indian Universities issues equivalence for the IB Diploma and for IGCSE-based qualifications, many central universities admit through CUET-UG, and JEE and NEET have eligibility rules that international-board students must check annually. Start the equivalence paperwork early in Class 12 and confirm each institution's own conditions." },
    { question: "Can lessons pause for Bihu, Doul, Durga Puja and Eid?", answer: "Yes. Families usually fix a weekday evening and a weekend slot, then pause or move sessions around Bohag Bihu, Doul, Durga Puja and Eid by agreement with the tutor. Because lessons are online, an extra session before a mock or exam series is easy to add and nobody has to travel to make up time." },
    { question: "What if the tutor is not the right fit?", answer: "Tell us and we will find another tutor. Progress is reviewed every few weeks, and a change is made whenever the fit is wrong, rather than asking a student to continue with someone who is not helping. The free trial lesson is designed to catch a mismatch early, and rates are in writing from the start." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any school or board named on this page?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service with no partnership, contract or endorsement from the International Baccalaureate, Cambridge International, Pearson or any school, college or university mentioned here. Those names appear only to describe real options for Barpeta families. Admission, exam entry and equivalence decisions belong to those bodies, not to us." },
  ],

